Everything is working end-to-end. Here's a summary of what was built:

## MS MARCO Passage Search App

**Backend (Anserini REST API)**
- Installed Anserini fatjar v2.1.1 from Maven Central
- Smoke tested with CACM index (MAP 0.3123, P30 0.1942 ✓)
- REST server running on port **8080** at `http://localhost:8080/v1/msmarco-v1-passage/search`

**Frontend (Next.js)**
- Running on port **3000** at `http://localhost:3000`
- Search input with "Search" button
- 5 randomly selected sample queries from the MS MARCO passage dev set displayed on each page load
- Click a sample query to run it instantly
- Ranked results shown with rank badge, docid, score, and passage text
- Handles empty queries, no-results, and backend errors with clear messages

**Configuration (`.env.local`)**
- `ANSERINI_URL` — backend URL (default `http://localhost:8080`)
- `SEARCH_HITS` — number of results (default `10`)
- Frontend port configurable via `PORT` env var (default `3000`)

**Key files:**
- `search-app/data/sample-queries.json` — 20 MS MARCO dev queries
- `search-app/app/api/search/route.ts` — API proxy to Anserini
- `search-app/app/SearchPage.tsx` — client-side search UI
- `search-app/app/page.tsx` — server component with random sample selection